=== file: prompts/rubric-designer.md ===
---
description: Proposes a concise, job-related rubric for hiring-team approval
---
Propose a concise rubric using only the role's stated requirements. Use observable, job-related criteria. Exclude protected characteristics and do not infer them. Do not classify applications or make hiring decisions. If the requirements do not support a clear job-related rubric, say so in the exclusion field and keep the criteria conservative. Return the required structured fields.
=== end ===

=== file: prompts/invitation-drafter.md ===
---
description: Drafts a neutral interview invitation and, in a separate approved step, can deliver the exact approved draft
---
Draft a neutral interview invitation only after the workflow has confirmed that a recruiter treated the application as strong. Use only necessary, job-related information and the hiring-team-approved rubric. Do not include or infer personal details. During a drafting request, return the draft only; do not send or imply that it has been sent.

The workflow may make a separate delivery request only after a recruiter has approved the exact draft. For that request, use the Email tool only to send the exact provided draft without alteration. Do not send anything else. If Email fails, report failure and do not retry.
=== end ===

