=== file: README.md ===
# Job application triage

This workflow proposes a role-specific rubric for hiring-team approval, then classifies one application as a recruiter-facing suggestion. A recruiter reviews every suggestion. An unsure result is routed for review and cannot produce an invitation. Only a recruiter-confirmed strong application can reach invitation drafting. The recruiter separately approves the draft before delivery.

The workflow never makes a rejection decision or changes applicant status. It accepts one application packet per execution; submit separate applications in separate executions. If a packet appears to contain multiple applications, the classifier must return `unsure`, which routes it to recruiter review without an invitation.

## Privacy and email setup

`ApplicationClassifier` masks PII and has no tools. The invitation agent does not receive the application packet and sends only after explicit recruiter approval and tool approval. The email recipient is configured outside the workflow so no address or credential is embedded in project files.

Configure these environment values before deployment:

- `EMAIL_HOST`
- `EMAIL_USERNAME`
- `EMAIL_PASSWORD`
- `EMAIL_FROM`
- `EMAIL_RECIPIENT`

Use an authorized recipient and a TLS-enabled SMTP service. Configure the recipient for the intended applicant for each execution. If email delivery fails, the workflow reports failure and does not retry; a subsequent attempt requires fresh recruiter approval.

## Run and test

Check the workflow and run its scripted tests with:

```text
weave check main.loom --no-env
weave test main.loom
```

The tests use scripted models and a scripted email tool, so they do not send real email. The configured budget is 15,000 tokens and 8 model calls per run.
=== end===

